{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 4,
  "simulation_id": "sim-03",
  "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B014",
        "laureates": [
          "Francis Halzen"
        ],
        "citation": "for establishing high-energy neutrino astronomy"
      },
      {
        "ballot_id": "B045",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and pioneering realization of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B036",
    "B007"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B014 recognizes an experimentally secured new window on the universe: high-energy neutrino astronomy has advanced from a difficult detection to a durable observational discipline. B045 recognizes a separate, sharply bounded physical advance: magic-wavelength confinement permits precision interrogation of many atoms without the usual motional compromise. Together these parts reward new access to nature, one astronomical and one metrological, while the proposed names remain compact and tied to the stated achievements.",
    "case_against": "The unresolved weakness of B014 is not its scientific maturity but individual attribution in a collaboration-scale enterprise. Francis Halzen should receive sole credit only if the historical record establishes an intellectually and institutionally decisive role rather than prominence within a collective success. For B045, the citation must not become recognition of successive clock records, broad optical-frequency metrology, or prospective applications. Each part must independently satisfy the prize threshold; pairing them cannot compensate for an attribution or boundary failure in either.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "pearce-mark",
        "point": "Pearce supports the B014-B045 pairing, describing high-energy neutrinos as a new durable messenger channel and optical lattice clocks as a mature physical advance, while emphasizing the IceCube attribution problem.",
        "response": "I agree with both assessments and retain the pairing for that reason. Pearce is right that the two achievements are independently substantial rather than merely complementary. But the IceCube issue remains a condition of the recommendation: a new messenger does not by itself identify a single laureate, so Halzen's distinctive foundational leadership must be demonstrated before the configuration is confirmed."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll argues that the magic-wavelength lattice-clock principle is more than exceptional instrument performance because it established a new precision-measurement regime, with unusually clear Katori-Ye attribution.",
        "response": "I find this the decisive clarification for B045. The prize-worthy content is the physical solution to a concrete systematic constraint, not a ranking of clock accuracy. I therefore adopt the more explicit invention-and-pioneering-realization wording, while retaining the strict boundary Kroll proposes around the lattice-clock principle."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson favors circuit QED because it identifies a controllable quantum-optics regime with a coherent Blais-Wallraff-Schoelkopf theory-experiment chain.",
        "response": "B007 remains my leading non-cosmological alternative because that chain is scientifically compelling and mature. I still place it below the preferred two parts: its citation boundary must be protected from the much broader collective development of superconducting quantum computing, whereas B045 can be confined more cleanly to the magic-wavelength lattice-clock advance."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical documentation establishes that Francis Halzen's intellectual and institutional leadership is individually decisive enough for sole credit for B014.",
      "Whether Katori and Ye alone fully delimit the foundational lattice-clock achievement and how narrowly the B045 citation can exclude broader optical-frequency metrology.",
      "Whether WMAP's distinct mission-scale contribution can be separated sufficiently clearly from later precision CMB work if B036 is reconsidered."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile. My theoretical work in cosmology and gravitation does not indicate a personal or institutional connection to any proposed laureate."
  }
}
